{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1558555-how-often-does-poison-come-up-in-your-games","id":1558555,"title":"How often does poison come up in your games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-02-27T23:00:21-08:00","id":1558555,"title":"How often does poison come up in your games?","content":"Basically the title. Poisoning drinks, poisoning weapons, poisoning with Charms - how often does poison get used in your campaigns, either by players or ST characters?<br /> <br /> My first big campaign, 2.5 Celestials, featured almost zero use of the poison rules - there was toxic gas in an underground section, and a couple enemies with venom that didn't amount to anything, but that's about it. Hardly even occurred as a worthwhile tool in the &quot;wandering heroes vs demons and deathknights&quot; romp.<br /> <br /> But now, a ways into our second major campaign, 3e DBs, we've taken to poison like fish to water. This game's a lot more human-focused and political, so more viable targets and fewer better alternatives for both sides of the conflict, and after a classic &quot;poisoned drinks into combat&quot; assassination attempt the players realized &quot;wow, that was brutal. I bet we can do it back worse!&quot; Our Wood Aspect naturally leans hardest into it, using a mix of regular and hallucinogenic poison to cause chaos while infiltrating enemy territory, and the Fire and Water Aspects have orchestrated a couple assassination attempts with it, but it's used most in combat, for the joy of stacking even more passive damage atop their anima flux, or to hinder back-line enemies (archers, sorcerers, generals, etc).<br /> <br /> They've developed a range of anti-poison strategies as well to protect themselves, ranging from the historic (our Water Aspect keeps a cupbearer) to the heroic (our Earth and Wood Aspects can preemptively detect or simply tank many poisons) to the mythic (our Fire Aspect has the Burning Branch Evocation for burning poisons out of people's bodies, and has saved a few lives with it). It led to a lot of interesting roleplay as the characters got shocked into a bout of paranoia and moral dilemma (mostly about whether letting the cupbearer do taste tests was okay) and then gradually mastered it themselves to protect allies and debilitate enemies.<br /> <br /> What about you guys? What have your campaign experiences with poison been like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28948-mj6373","name":"MJ6373","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-28T00:33:22-08:00","id":1558556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MJ6373</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1558555-how-often-does-poison-come-up-in-your-games#post1558555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically the title. Poisoning drinks, poisoning weapons, poisoning with Charms - how often does poison get used in your campaigns, either by players or ST characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm playing with the Essence ruleset. Poison came up twice in my games, both times against NPCs because tbh it doesn't have enough teeth against PCs I feel. One was a assassination attempt against a PC ally, so they found out about it and had to cure it and find the culprit. The other was a successful assassination attempt against the Ysiri Ambassador to Champoor (a PC is playing the new ambassador) so they had investigate who's guilty of it (they haven't found that out yet, we play in a few hours XD).<br /> <br /> None of my PCs ever use poisons against their enemies -- yet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2314-salinea","name":"salinea","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}